{
  "description": "Cross-player active-hours cases (docs/settings.md, docs/browser-player.md). Each case is a Player configuration `power` section, an instant, and the result of the active-hours policy at that instant. The shared TypeScript policy (packages/player-active-hours, used by the Linux Player and the Browser Player) and Player Core (crates/player-core/tests/active_hours_contract.rs) must both produce exactly `expected`. `msUntilTransition` counts minutes of the local clock, so across a daylight saving change it can be an hour from the real transition; the caller evaluates again when it expires. The cases cover the same-day and overnight windows, the half-open end, listed weekdays, every fail-open misconfiguration, and the daylight saving gap and overlap in both hemispheres. Regenerate `expected` from the TypeScript policy with `TILECAST_ACTIVE_HOURS_WRITE=1 npm test --workspace @tilecast/player-active-hours` then run `npx prettier --write` on this file and review the diff.",
